        T("Application", "Flight Data",
            "Monitor the active vehicle through the HUD, mission map and telemetry panels, and access supported vehicle commands. Reset model heading captures a display-only reference for the HUD heading arrow; Restore heading removes it. The 2D cockpit horizon and compass remain unchanged. Fresh attitude is required; changing vehicle/session clears the reference.",
            "Confirm the vehicle identity, connection state and live telemetry before interpreting displayed values.|Use Quick and Gauges for selected readings, Status for detailed telemetry, and Messages for vehicle-reported information and warnings.|Review PreFlight before operation. Use Actions only after checking the requested command and target.|To access storage as a USB drive on compatible controllers and firmware, keep the vehicle disarmed and select Actions > Reboot to USB storage. Review and confirm the restart; the action is unavailable when the reboot checks are not satisfied.|Connect by USB and check whether the operating system exposes the controller's storage. When finished, safely eject the drive and restart the controller to return to normal operation, then reconnect telemetry.|Servo/Relay, Aux Function and Payload Control can affect connected hardware; review output assignments and keep mechanisms clear.|Use DataFlash Logs for the vehicle's onboard recordings; use the separate Logs workspace for PC telemetry recordings and application diagnostics.",
            "Check fresh telemetry and the vehicle's reported state after a command. For USB storage, read the command result and verify that the drive actually appears. A command acknowledgement or lost telemetry connection alone does not prove that storage mounted successfully.",
            "Reboot to USB storage interrupts telemetry and control and requires compatible firmware and hardware. It runs only when you request and confirm it. Use Configuration > Mavlink Ftp for file access over a supported telemetry connection instead. Recorded or stale data is not live vehicle evidence. Review Scripts before execution and remove propellers for bench actuator checks.",
            "https://ardupilot.org/planner/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.html"),
